---
// DIAGRAM for 1.1: the analyst's loop. A business question becomes data, a summary, an honest range of
// uncertainty and then a decision, which raises the next question.
---
<figure class="cs-fig mlf">
  <span class="cs-figtag">The analyst's loop</span>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 640 230" role="img" aria-label="Five boxes in a loop: question, data, describe, measure uncertainty, decide, and back to question">
    <defs><marker id="st-ar" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="fa" /></marker></defs>
    <rect class="acc" x="10" y="20" width="160" height="62" rx="10" /><text x="90" y="46" text-anchor="middle" class="b">1. Question</text><text x="90" y="66" text-anchor="middle" class="mu">Did the promo lift sales?</text>
    <rect class="box" x="240" y="20" width="160" height="62" rx="10" /><text x="320" y="46" text-anchor="middle" class="b">2. Data</text><text x="320" y="66" text-anchor="middle" class="mu">Which rows, which period?</text>
    <rect class="box" x="470" y="20" width="160" height="62" rx="10" /><text x="550" y="46" text-anchor="middle" class="b">3. Describe</text><text x="550" y="66" text-anchor="middle" class="mu">Averages, spread, charts</text>
    <rect class="box" x="470" y="148" width="160" height="62" rx="10" /><text x="550" y="174" text-anchor="middle" class="b">4. Uncertainty</text><text x="550" y="194" text-anchor="middle" class="mu">Real, or just noise?</text>
    <rect class="acc" x="240" y="148" width="160" height="62" rx="10" /><text x="320" y="174" text-anchor="middle" class="b">5. Decide</text><text x="320" y="194" text-anchor="middle" class="mu">Keep, stop or test more</text>
    <path class="lna" d="M170 51 H236" marker-end="url(#st-ar)" /><path class="lna" d="M400 51 H466" marker-end="url(#st-ar)" />
    <path class="lna" d="M550 82 V144" marker-end="url(#st-ar)" /><path class="lna" d="M470 179 H404" marker-end="url(#st-ar)" />
    <path class="lna" d="M240 179 H90 V86" marker-end="url(#st-ar)" /><text x="100" y="170" class="mu">next question</text>
    <text x="632" y="226" text-anchor="end" class="wm">fibub.com</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>Statistics lives in steps 3 and 4. Describing data says what happened in the rows you have; measuring uncertainty says how much of that would change with different rows. Most bad business decisions skip step 4.</figcaption>
</figure>
